Z||000000||Denise||05-24-2000||11:37 AM||||I've obtained a 120 speedometer. should go right in,  right? Yes i've had the thing apart a few times with changeing cables, shifters, gauges, bulbs, etc.. <BR> <BR>Also i'm going to 15 inch lace wheels soon, with 205's and 215's,  do I need a Different gear for the speed sensor?  <P>I'm running stock 86 turbo wheels now. (they are for sale)with Radial TA's ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||05-24-2000||12:55 PM||||Not too long ago someone posted a message about finding an electronic gadget that allows you to dial in adjustments to the speedometer to account for different tire sizes.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||05-24-2000||12:58 PM||||I have an 86 SE that I just put in an 87 GT dash (120 speedo) There is no changes other than the speedo. As for tire sizes. There is only a .2% error difference between your stock wheels and tires and the stock sizes for the GT. You do not have to change the speedo gear unless you are going a lot larger or a lot smaller than stock size tires and you want the speedo acurate. You can just get your error % and that can guide you also. If you click on this link you just select your original size and the size you are going to and it gives you the speedo error in percentages below as well as all the measurements of the tires.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.secret-secret.com/turbo/DIY/tirecalc/turbotire.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.secret-secret.com/turbo/DIY/tirecalc/turbotire.html</A> <BR>||||reg||1
